=== under -v the live line names the test and its position
--- header
mylib: 2 tests
--- begin_test
«erase»«d|  Running [1/2] math › addition…» [no newline]
--- result
«erase»  «g|PASS»  math › addition                            «d|0.2ms»

=== a compact run's live line draws from column zero and never brings the header out
--- header
--- begin_test
«erase»«d|  [1/2] math › addition…» [no newline]
--- a pass
--- begin_test
«erase»«erase»«d|  [2/2] users › sessions after login…» [no newline]

=== the live line is erased before a block and redrawn under it
--- header
--- begin_test
«erase»«d|  [1/2] bad…» [no newline]
--- a failure
«erase»mylib: 2 tests
«d|──────────────────────── failures ────────────────────────»
  «r|FAIL»  «b|bad»
    b
--- begin_test
«erase»«d|  [2/2] math › addition…» [no newline]
--- a pass

=== a live name's control bytes print escaped
--- header
--- begin_test
«erase»«d|  [1/2] first\x0ahalf…» [no newline]

=== a compact run's notice is the live line, erased before the summary
--- header
--- a pass
--- begin_test
«erase»«d|  [2/2] b…» [no newline]
--- note
«erase»«d|releasing db» [no newline]
--- finish
«erase»s: «g|1 passed», 1 not run in 10ms.

